<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Memphis is top cargo airport in Q1,97.</title>
<headline>ACI says Memphis is top cargo airport in Q1,97.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express Corp, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-March 1997, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in its latest survey of 495 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January-March 1997, with the volume they handled, their ranking and the percentage change on January-March 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1 (1)   Memphis	    513,351		up 18.7 pct</p>
<p>    2 (3)   Los Angeles	436,281		up  9.2</p>
<p>    3 (2)   Miami		412,034		up  0.3</p>
<p>    4 (4)   Narita	     407,424		up  7.1</p>
<p>    5 (8)   Hong Kong	  389,993		up 17.7</p>
<p>    6 (5)   JFK		  386,296		up  2.5</p>
<p>    7 (6)   Frankfurt	  365,556		up  2.3</p>
<p>    8 (9)   Seoul		361,728		up 19.7</p>
<p>    9 (7)   Louisville	 331,588	    down  2.5</p>
<p>    10(12)  Singapore	  317,933		up 14.5</p>
<p>    11(11)  Chicago	    309,437		up 11.3</p>
<p>    12(10)  Amsterdam	  291,260		up  3.8</p>
<p>    13(13)  Heathrow	   284,133		up  4.7</p>
<p>    14(16)  Anchorage*	 279,684		up 23.8</p>
<p>    15(14)  Paris CDG	  243,907		up  4.8</p>
<p>    16(15)  Newark	     238,868		up  5.5</p>
<p>    17(19)  Taipei	     201,419		up 18.7</p>
<p>    18(17)  Atlanta	    196,829		up  2.6</p>
<p>    19(20)  Dayton	     191,183		up  6.6</p>
<p>    20(18)  Dallas Ft.Worth  188,948		up  8.3</p>
<p>* includes freight and mail in transit as well as loaded  + unloaded - ACI FROM STUART TODD</p>
</text>
